.SH EXAMPLES
Set up \fBiocell\fP from scratch:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell activate ZPOOL
    iocell fetch release=15.1-RELEASE

.fam T
.fi
Create first jail:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell create release=15.1-RELEASE tag=myjail vnet=off

.fam T
.fi
List jails:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell list

.fam T
.fi
Start jail:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell start UUID

.fam T
.fi
Turn on resource \fIlimits\fP and apply them:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell set rlimits=on UUID
    iocell cap UUID

.fam T
.fi
Display resource usage:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell inuse UUID

.fam T
.fi
Convert jail into template:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell set istemplate=yes UUID

.fam T
.fi
List templates:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell list -t

.fam T
.fi
Clone jail from template:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell clone TAG-of-template tag=myjail

.fam T
.fi
Import a compatible trusted image on another host
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell import UUID

.fam T
.fi
Get the last successful \fIstart\fP time for all jails
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    iocell get -r last_started

.fam T
.fi
.SH HINTS
The active pool is recorded in UCL \fIdefaults\fP; legacy discovery can also use
a pool comment. Do not assume \fIdeactivate\fP clears either selection mechanism.
.PP
VNET requires an appropriate bridge, routing and firewall policy. A physical
bridge member can expose jail MACs upstream. If a provider prohibits extra
MACs, use a private bridge with host routing/NAT instead; \fBiocell\fP does not
automatically configure that NAT. Preserve management access while testing.
.PP
Per-jail firewall support depends on the host kernel, permissions and device
exposure; verify these capabilities on the host.
Do not blindly disable bridge filtering or IPv6 duplicate-address detection.
.PP
Validate actual properties and kernel behavior for your host release.
Remaining \fIcommand\fP defects are documented in the repository's known issues.
.PP
The actual jail name in the \fBjls\fP(8) output is \fIset\fP to ioc-UUID. This is a
required workaround as jails will refuse to \fIstart\fP with \fBjail\fP(8) when name
starts with a "0".
.PP
To prevent dmesg leak inside jails apply the following sysctl:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    security.bsd.unprivileged_read_msgbuf=0

.fam T
.fi
Enable forwarding only when the host is intentionally routing jail traffic,
and configure bridge filtering and NAT for your security boundary. There is
no universally safe \fIset\fP of pfil sysctls to copy into every host.
.PP
For more information please visit:
.PP
.nf
.fam C
    https://github.com/iocell/iocell

.fam T
.fi
